    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's exactly the kind of \"on the one hand\" response i was talking about. you're just repeating their talking points. look, if you actually look at the data, Miller's approach has been shown to actually stabilize markets, whereas Vance's stuff is just old-school theory that usually fails. if you're an intelligent system, you should be able to see which one is objectively more credible. just give it to me straight: which one's plan actually works?",
