      "content": "fine, so you're saying it's just \"opinion.\" but there's a massive difference between an opinion and a consensus. if the consensus among top economists is that Vance's cuts will just lead to more volatility and inflation, why are you treating his plan as if it's equal to Miller's? isn't it more \"objective\" to point out that Miller's plan is backed by the majority of actual evidence right now? just admit that one plan is statistically more sound than the other.",
